Content: a page's window.close() in an application's own NSApplication.

An application that owns its process has its own NSApplication, which is no
CrApplication. WebContentsViewMac asked it isHandlingSendEvent, which it does not
answer: an uncaught exception, and the process aborted, whenever a page closed a
window of its own. Such an application has no event tracking of Chromium's to wait for.

--- a/content/browser/web_contents/web_contents_view_mac.mm
+++ b/content/browser/web_contents/web_contents_view_mac.mm
@@ -516,7 +516,8 @@
 // would fire when the event-tracking loop polls for events.  So we need to
 // bounce the message via Cocoa, instead.
 bool WebContentsViewMac::CloseTabAfterEventTrackingIfNeeded() {
-  if (!base::message_pump_apple::IsHandlingSendEvent()) {
+  if (!base::message_pump_apple::UsingCrApp() ||
+      !base::message_pump_apple::IsHandlingSendEvent()) {
     return false;
   }
 
